<title>FRANCE: US MAIN JAN-JUNE EX-PARIS AIR CARGO EXPORT ROUTE.</title>
<headline>US MAIN JAN-JUNE EX-PARIS AIR CARGO EXPORT ROUTE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. was the principal destination for export traffic from the Paris airports in January-June 1997, Paris airport authority (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>In January-June 1997 export traffic from Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 287,592 tonnes, an increase of 1.9 percent on the same period last year.</p>
<p>The 20 top destinations by country for ADP exports in January-June 1997, with percentage change on January-June 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>     Destination	Tonnes   Pct Change</p>
<p>					 1996</p>
<p>    1. United States   63,728   up  4.7</p>
<p>    2. Japan	     15,191 down  8.3</p>
<p>    3. Hong Kong	 12,356   up 11.7</p>
<p>    4. Germany	   11,796   up 24.6</p>
<p>    5. Canada	    10,129 down  4.7</p>
<p>    6. UK		   9,497   up 25.0</p>
<p>    7. U.A.E		7,917   up  6.1</p>
<p>    8. Brazil	     7,788   up 13.4</p>
<p>    9. India		6,801 down  5.8</p>
<p>   10. Mexico	     6,528   up 16.9</p>
<p>   11. Fr.W Indies	5,859 down  3.9</p>
<p>   12. Singapore	  5,594   up 39.9</p>
<p>   13. Reunion	    4,964   up  0.4</p>
<p>   14. Saudi Arabia     4,784 down 10.2</p>
<p>   15. Egypt		4,257 down  2.7</p>
<p>   16. Thailand	   3,879   up  5.6</p>
<p>   17. Italy		3,853 down 17.6</p>
<p>   18. Lebanon	    3,690   up  2.6</p>
<p>   19. China		3,636 down  5.3</p>
<p>   20. Korea		3,634 down  7.9</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
